I think the problem with the banes having double damage against a
cohort of monsters is that these monsters are early game and
(generally) by the time you have the scrolls of enchant weapon ready
to exploit the double damage you don't need it anymore, because the
monsters aren't an issue.

That's the reason I originally suggested insta-killing monsters,
because it actually makes it useful for low level characters.

I do really agree with you though that instakilling is very cheesy and
not something that happens often in the normal game, but I was stuck
in providing usefulness to characters without enchantment.  What is
left? Extra base damage? What if the banes had a +d20 (or even +d30?)
like silver damage on top of their 2x damage.  You could have
appropriate messages like silver damage does as well.

